  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w600.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-W 654.07 Income-In-Kind",
  "priorExpiration": "1997-10-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 654.07 Income-In-Kind.\n\n(a) For all adult categories of financial assistance, earned income-in-kind received on a regular basis shall be assigned a dollar value and shall be treated as countable earned income as follows:\n\n(1) The dollar value shall be determined by a statement from the employer indicating the frequency and dollar value of earned income-in-kind, or, if unable to obtain such a statement, by multiplying the number of hours worked times the hourly wage as provided by the employer;\n\n(2) If the employer is unable to provide an approximate hourly wage, or the client is self-employed, the current minimum hourly wage shall be used; and\n\n(3) From the dollar value amount determined as referenced in (1) or (2) above, any monetary payment received as a supplement for the same job shall be subtracted, resulting in gross earned income-in-kind.\n\n(b) With the exception of payments made from trusts or similar legal devices, for adult category financial assistance, unearned income-in-kind shall represent a component of the adult category standard of need and shall not be counted as income.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at Chapter Heading He-W 600) #5171, eff 6-26-91; amd by #6111, eff 11-1-95; ss by #6531, INTERIM, eff 6-27-97, EXPIRES: 10-25-97\n\nNew. #6740, eff 4-25-98; ss by #8596, eff 3-30-06; ss by #10563, eff 3-30-14; ss by #13929, eff 4-24-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w600.html"
